VERSION 1.9.0 — Category System Integration

Features
- Added full category management system (create, edit, delete)
- Introduced categories.json as configuration registry
- Categories now auto-generated from topic data
- Added category dialog UI (mirrors subcategory management)
- Integrated Cat_Icon support across system

Improvements
- Unified data architecture using app.APP_DATA (removed global state inconsistencies)
- Improved startup flow with async-safe taxonomy generation
- Synchronized category and subcategory generation logic

Fixes
- Fixed race condition where taxonomy generation ran before Firebase data was loaded
- Fixed inconsistent data access between services and UI
- Corrected icon fallback behaviour when Cat_Icon missing

VERSION 1.8.0 — Dialog System & Architecture Refactor

Improvements
Refactored main application architecture with clear separation between UI, dialogs, and services
Reduced complexity in main.py by delegating UI logic to dedicated dialog components
Improved maintainability through centralised dialog handling system
Enhanced code readability with cleaner responsibility boundaries (App → Services → UI)
Improved consistency of popup behaviour across the application
Streamlined icon handling using unified icon service

Features
Introduced reusable dialog system:

cleanup_dialog
confirm_dialog
promotion_dialog

Added centralised cleanup dialog with preview, delete, and undo workflow
Added reusable confirmation dialog component for destructive actions
Added reusable promotion dialog for topic publishing workflow
Integrated dedicated icon service for resolving, copying, and managing assets
Modularised topic promotion/demotion logic into service layer
Improved extensibility for future UI components and dialogs

Fixes
Fixed inconsistent popup behaviour caused by duplicate inline implementations
Resolved cleanup dialog rendering inconsistencies
Fixed icon handling duplication across multiple modules
Fixed multiple sources of UI state inconsistencies in main.py
Removed legacy popup code paths causing maintenance issues
Improved stability of delete and promotion workflows

VERSION 1.7.0 — UI System & AppWindow Upgrade

Improvements

Introduced resizable application window with dynamic layout scaling
Added top-aligned window positioning for improved desktop usability
Stabilised window behaviour across Linux environments (Arch, Ubuntu)
Improved overall UI consistency through unified popup styling
Enhanced spacing, typography, and layout balance across screens
Improved first-run experience with automatic runtime configuration setup

Features

Implemented reusable themed popup system across the application
Added unified file picker component (used for icons, screenshots, configuration files)
Introduced consistent popup design matching application theme
Enabled Firebase read access without requiring service account key
Added automatic Firebase configuration initialisation on first run
Improved AppImage packaging workflow with fully working distribution build

Fixes

Fixed window resizing instability and recursive resize crash
Fixed window positioning issues causing incorrect default placement
Fixed inconsistent popup styling across different screens
Fixed file picker UI (oversized buttons, small text, default styling)
Fixed missing firebase.json causing empty data on first run
Resolved AppImage runtime configuration path issues
Fixed inconsistencies in cache and Firebase fallback behaviour

